The diagram is drawn by the candidate (large, neat, title *Longitudinal section of the human heart*, ruled label lines). It shows:

- four chambers: **right atrium** and **left atrium** (thin walls, at the top), **right ventricle** and **left ventricle** (thick walls, at the bottom; the wall of the left ventricle is the thickest);
- the **septum** separating the right side from the left side;
- the **tricuspid valve** (between the right atrium and the right ventricle) and the **bicuspid (mitral) valve** (between the left atrium and the left ventricle), with the **tendinous cords** (heart strings) attached to **papillary muscles** of the ventricle wall;
- the **semilunar valves** at the base of the pulmonary artery and of the aorta;
- the **superior and inferior vena cava** entering the right atrium;
- the **pulmonary artery** leaving the right ventricle;
- the **pulmonary veins** entering the left atrium;
- the **aorta** leaving the left ventricle;
- (optional) the **coronary arteries** on the surface of the heart.

Marking: correct shape and proportions, and at least six correct labels.
